\par \sect }\sectd \psz9\linex0\cols2\colsx288\linebetcol\sectdefaultcl \pard\plain \s16\sl-259\slmult0\widctlpar\adjustright \b\fs28\lang2057 {The House of the Rising Sun 
\par }\pard\plain \widctlpar\adjustright \fs20\lang2057 {
\par There is a house in New Orleans 
\par They call the Rising Sun 
\par And it\rquote s been the ruin of many poor girl, 
\par And me, oh God, for one. 
\par 
\par If I had listened to what my mother said, 
\par I\rquote d have been at home today, 
\par But I was young and foolish, oh God, 
\par Let a rambler lead me astray. 
\par 
\par Go tell my baby sister, 
\par Don\rquote t do what I have done 
\par But shun that house in New Orleans 
\par They call the Rising Sun. 
\par 
\par I\rquote m goin\rquote  back to New Orleans 
\par My race is almost run, 
\par I\rquote m goin\rquote  back to spend my life 
\par Beneath that Rising Sun. 
\par 
\par 
\par 
\par }\pard\plain \s16\sl-259\slmult0\widctlpar\adjustright \b\fs28\lang2057 {St James\rquote  Infirmary 
\par }\pard\plain \widctlpar\adjustright \fs20\lang2057 {
\par }{\i Version I 
\par }{Folks, I\rquote m goin\rquote  down to St. James Infirmary, 
\par See my baby there; 
\par She\rquote s stretched out on a long, white table, 
\par She\rquote s so sweet, so cold, so fair. 
\par Let her go, let her go, God bless her, 
\par Wherever she may be, 
\par She will search this wide world over, 
\par But she\rquote ll never find another sweet man like me. 
\par Now, when I die, bury me in my straight-leg britches, 
\par Put on a box-back coat and a stetson hat, 
\par Put a twenty-dollar gold piece on my watch chain, 
\par So you can let all the boys know I died standing pat. 
\par Folks, now that you have heard my story, 
\par Say, boy, hand me another shot of that booze; 
\par If anyone should ask you, 
\par Tell \lquote em I\rquote ve got those St. James Infirmary}{\b  }{blues. 
\par 
\par }{\i Version 2 
\par }{I went down to St. James Infirmary, 
\par Saw my baby there, 
\par Set down on a long white table, 
\par So sweet, so cold, so fair. 
\par Let her go, let her go, God bless her, 
\par Wherever she may be, 
\par She can look this wide world over, 
\par She\rquote ll never find}{\b  }{a sweet man like me. 
